In the UNIX and OVMS space, I would assume so. There's an installed base
of close to 500K servers.


Or is it a black hole where money is dumped. If it were a gold
> mine, DEC wouldn't have gone down the drain like that. 

DEC's confrontation with the Roto-Rooter man had multiple causes. The
Alpha **architecture** was not among the most prominent of these.

Striking a mother lode and actually extracting and smelting the ore are
two different things. DEC screwed up big-time on the "smelting" front.

