hi

I recently bought 2 VX40 Multia from http://www.cpumicromart.com/ as
well as 64 megs or RAM for one of these machines. None of them has been
able to bootup. 2 have been sent to me as replacement, which doesn't
work better.

2 machines display the white cursor on the bottom-left corner, and 2
machines doesn't even activate the video signal. The SROM LED doesn't
report anything strange... and also flashes 14 times if I remove the
RAM, as expected. BTW, the SROM flash is exactly the same on the
"working" (cursor on the screen) and non-working machines.

One of the machines has been able to do some checks, once. I took some
notes:

** BL3 x3.5-72
** 
** testing memory from 800000 to 3d0000
** sys_pci_allocate_vector failed: DEV_SEL is 0x0 , DEV_INT_PIN is 0x0
** Unexpected Machine Check through vector 00000067

I also have full dump of the registers, but I'm not sure they're
relevant.

I tried to boot with the failsafe disk... and it doesn't work either
(screen remains black, the floppy doesn't ever stop to spin).

The battery is new, has been tested, and is ok. The power supply is ok.

After several calls to try to get support, I must admit that in the
future, I won't buy anything from this company. My RMA request has
been lost 2 times... and they never returned any of my calls...

I'm suspecting a RAM problem, since it's the only common factor in the
4 machines, and even if I don't trust cpumicromart, it's fairly
improbable that they sent me 4 non-working machines.

I'm looking for a RAM supplier that does supply RAM that has been
tested for the multia, or if you can, the description of the RAM that's
inside your box... chip numbers, count, ...

If anyone has thoughts to share, experiments ideas... feel free to reply
(news & mail).

thanks in advance

  alex



