  This would not suprise me.  At a computer conference in the late 80's
  the keynote talk was from a leading edge company doing computer animation
  for movie effects and commercials.  They showed a short clip of their
  work and gave some statistics on render time on a Cray.  As people were
  strolling out of the ballroom for lunch I was passed by three middle
  aged gentleman with IBM on their name tags.  I overhead one of them
  ask "What's a Cray?"  The second man shrugged while the third said
  he thought it was a large computer.  The first asked "Is it as fast as
  a 3081?"  The third man said he doubt it.

  To be fair much of IBM now is outward looking and customer driven but
  in an organization that large there are probably still pockets of the
  old culture left.

