Phillip Helbig wrote:
> 
> I have a VAXstation 3100 M38 which I'm trying to boot as a satellite off
> a VAXstation 4000 M60.  A 3100 M30 bots fine as a satellite.  After
> setting up the M38 the same way, it doesn't boot.  Perhaps because of
> self-test errors?
> 
> KA42-V  V1.5
> 
> F..E..D  etc
> 
> ?  C  0080  0000.4001
> ?  6  80A1  0000.4001
> 
> Any ideas?  What do the errors actually mean?
> 
> Other than being an M38 instead of an M30, the only difference between
> the machines is that the M38 has two SCSI controllers and an RZ23L disk.

I was with Phillip when we were trying this. This was the setup: A
VAXstation 4000/60 set up as a boot node running OpenVMS 7.1, but with
no DECnet, so we were using LACACP etc to remote boot satellites. We
configured a VAXstation 3100/30 as a satellite and it booted fine. When
we tried a VAXstation 3100/38, it sta there attempting to boot but never
succeeding. There were no error messages on the 3100/38. OPCOM on the
4000 repeatedly produced a message saying it was volunteering to
download the relevant boot file for the satellite, but it obviously
never did.

One thing I noticed, was that the 3100/30 was using a V3 MOP request and
the 3100/38 was doing a V4 MOP request. So we modified the configuration
using LANCP for the satellite to say force V3 behaviour. In this set up,
the satellite appeared to send out about 4 V4 requests and then a V3
request, but the V3 request was not honoured either, and the satellite
went back to V4 requests and so on.

We also tried setting up a 4000/90 as a satellite and that exhibited the
same behaviour. We managed to get the 4000/90 to boot off a local hard
disk without any problem, so I'm convinced the problem is related to the
MOP version number.

Any ideas?

Tony Arnold.



