"Terry C. Shannon" wrote:
> Now, if only VMS ran on IA32... I could say "Hasta La Vista, SLAGWARE!"

Since the 8086 is as dead as the vax (the 8086 will *eventually* be replaced
by merced, right ?), it would be pointless at this time to port VMS to the 8086.

But making VMS boot on low end ALPHA stations and making VMS software
affordable and very competitive with its competing MS software would go a long
way. I would rather see an "official" cheap VMS than Compaq having to
volunteer a free but limited VMS to home weirdos (which I am).

One expands a market to low end business which may grow into good Compaq VMS
customers, while the other just postpones the inevitable throwing of old
hardware in the big non-binary bin and in the meantime just increases the
*VAX* freebie software base, something which Compaq would rather see increase
the ALPHA freeware base..



