Phillip Helbig wrote:
> 
> I have a VAXstation 3100 M38 which I'm trying to boot as a satellite off
> a VAXstation 4000 M60.  A 3100 M30 bots fine as a satellite.  After
> setting up the M38 the same way, it doesn't boot.  Perhaps because of
> self-test errors?

It would REALLY, REALLY help if you told us the error message you
got when you attempted to boot (from the RZ23?  from Ethernet?)

> KA42-V  V1.5
> 
> F..E..D  etc
> 
> ?  C  0080  0000.4001

Mouse and/or LK-series keyboard not found.

> ?  6  80A1  0000.4001

SCSI bus problem.  Do you have the terminator plugged into the
back?

Neither of these errors should stop you from booting.  Just do
a "B ESA0" and it should request a download over the Ethernet
(you'll see it asking for this if you log into the VS4000 as
SYSTEM and do a REPLY/ENABLE).

Tim.



