Phillip Helbig wrote:
> 
> I have a VAXstation 3100 M38 which I'm trying to boot as a satellite off
> a VAXstation 4000 M60.  A 3100 M30 bots fine as a satellite.  After
> setting up the M38 the same way, it doesn't boot.  Perhaps because of
> self-test errors?
> 
> KA42-V  V1.5
> 
> F..E..D  etc
> 
> ?  C  0080  0000.4001
> ?  6  80A1  0000.4001
> 
> Any ideas?  What do the errors actually mean?

Speaking from memory, I think the "C" error may occur if you are using a
terminal as your console.  It is basically warning you that one of the
serial ports did not get tested because it was already in use.

The "6" error is for one of you SCSI channels.  The line following it in
the "T 50" output would be useful, but it may be that you have a SCSI
bus which is not terminated or doesn't have anything connected.  Do you
have the internal SCSI cable in place?

Good luck!

