There is a Hobbiest license, HOWEVER it is only for fairly old versions of
the OS's running in the version of the PDP-11 emulator written by Bob
Supnik.  The emulator images that are available are only available for this
emulator and are not to be used with other emulators or on real Hardware. 
The license also covers at least some of the old versions of the layered
products, but I'm not aware of them being available anywhere.

Unfortunatly there isn't anything like the VMS Hobbiest License for those of
use that own PDP-11's :^(

Depending on the model of PDP-11 that you have, you might be able to run a
version of UNIX on your system.  SCO offers a source license for $100 that
will allow you to run the old AT&T and BSD versions of UNIX, once you have
this license there are people that can provide you with a copy of UNIX.



