> >   Given the operating frequency and power dissipation I think
> >   of it as a semiconductor magnetron.
> 
> Well, how much power does it actually radiate?  (Not counting radiated
> heat--I mean microwaves)

   Now that's the rub isn't it?  The FCC (or whoever) gets mighty mad if
   you radiate even a little (even a few mW, depending on the band).

   The magic is in the little details of board level design.  Basically
   you want to avoid attaching an antenna to a high frequency and/or fast
   edge rate signal.  So the Alpha is attached to a high quality PCB with
   plenty of power and ground planes.  The fast system bus interface
   signals (up to 333 MHz) are kept short, point-to point, and low swing
   with moderate edge rates (HSTL?).


> 
> PeterM

