In article <QHLA2.233$S31.579018@news.bctel.net>, "Nick Hone" <nhone@hotmail.com> writes:
:Has anyone had any luck installing Windows NT 4.0 on a DEC 2000 Model 300
:(aka Jensen, DECpc AXP 150) with an Adaptec AHA-1742A SCSI card?  When I
:try, the kernel crashes with an INACCESSIBLE_BOOT_DEVICE error with code 7B.

  The underlying configuration used in the Jensen -- variously known as 
  the DECpc AXP 150 in ARC console garb or as the DEC 2000 model 300 in 
  ARC or SRM console garb, and (with more expansion within the enclosure)
  as the DEC 2000 model 500 -- is very sensitive to the SCSI configuration.
  Substituting SCSI widgets for those sold with and tested with the Jensen
  configuration -- or extending the SCSI outside the box -- is not 
  something that I would recommend attempting.  (I will assume the ARC
  has configured an interrupt for the boot device, etc.)

 -------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
 Hoff (Stephen) Hoffman   OpenVMS Engineering   hoffman#xdelta.zko.dec.com




