Woe be unto those who attempt to ask penetrating questions of Intel. I
tried it during the June 3, 1994 P7 vaporware announcement and Intel was
not amused.

At that time, all Intel would say is that P7 would be "better than
Alpha," much faster (of course!) than Alpha, and that shipments would
begin in 1997.

Intel would NOT produce a roadmap, discuss its design teams, etc. You
know, simple and obvious stuff like that. But hey, if Intel says it, it
must be true, right? That's the way the announcement was reported by all
and sundry.

So it was said, so it was written, and so shall it be written (no
doubt!) in the future.

