Now if you assume that Alpha scales linear to 1 GHz, too, then the
Pentium-III looks not that hot even for integer. Of course, you can't
say that as you work for Compaq and everybody in the intel NG would
scream 'Vapour!', but I can get away comparing vapour to vapour :-)

I could even bring up the upper limit on the number of CPUs for SMP
boxes etc. Oh well, we'll see.

The only advantage I can see for my own use of Intel chips is that it
runs my client OS of choice (OS/2) and since not even IBM pulled their
heads out of their arses to get the PowerPC version to the market I have
no hope that it will ever run on Alpha. But for number crunching, why
take an Intel chip if you can get something faster for you money?


