giorgio.sangalli@omnitel.it writes:

> Hello.
> 
> During installation of Ghostscript 5.50 on Alpha Server with O.S. DEC Unix
> 4.0d when make was running I received this error message:
> 
> cc  -O	-I. -I./obj -Izlib  -o ./obj/szlibc.o -c ./szlibc.c cc: Error:
> ./szlibc.c, line 34: In this declaration, the type of "st_zlib_state" is not
> compatible with the type of a previous declaration of "st_zlib_state" at line
> number 47 in file ./szlibx.h. public_st_zlib_state();

Always build with the -std or -std1 CFLAGS. This forces DEC C to run
in ANSI mode instead of K&R. Then use the unixansi.mak file.

setenv CFLAGS "-fast -std1";make -f unixansi.mak

This did the trick for me.
