:
:I assume you're talking about "VMS-on-Mach"...

  The expected profits vs the cost of the work was a central factor.

  This was an advanced development project -- I was peripherally involved, 
  via the work that Chris Kaler was doing -- and the core tradeoffs involved 
  the redesign of most anything that tied into the kernel vs the expected 
  level of performance to be achieved (equal or better performance would 
  have been a basic requirement, had this work gone "live") vs the perceived 
  benefits of the kernel.  

  Modular vs Monolithic kernel implementations have been one of those areas 
  in computing architecture that oscillates, with proponents on both sides.
  As usual, there are benefits to both approaches -- finding the correct
  balance betweem these two techniques in any implementation is the trick...

