csabah@easy.com.au wrote:
>      is 4.0A. The problem relates to file attachments which come from
>      other mail packages ( yes, the MS PC Mail crap crept upon us here
>      as well .) The error message:
> 
>      "Document with ".RTF" file type cannot be displayed"
> 
>      Then at the bottom of the screen some other line:
> 
>      "shareable images must be installed to run privileged image"

The first message (.RTF file type) is normal as ALLIN1 does not know how to
display this file type on a character cell terminal. The second message
indicates that perhaps ALLIN1 tried to invoke the CDA converter library (or
some other conversion software) which was not setup properly on that machine
and thus the failure.

Typing [GOLD] W    (GOLD = PF1 on numeric keypad) will usually display a more
complete message which may also give you which file needs to be installed.

You can do IA (index of attachements), then DETACH the attachement and then
export it to a VMS file name and play with the RTF as you wish.

You can see what ALLIN1 is attempting to do by enabling tracing (I think it is
GOLD %), and after the message has been displayed press CTRL-B and you get a
log of all of what A1 tried to do). You'll probably see which file (script or
.COM) ALLIN1 invoked to do doc conversion and by looking at that file, you'll
get a better idea.



