piotrek <pwoj@cst.tpsa.pl> wrote:
> Hello
> J have qestion:
> Could  I run  programs on dec 4.0e  which was  compiled under dec 3.2g ?

> Need  I  recompile them ?

> Piter


For all practical purposes and programs that do not dig too deep into system 
internals, the answer is 'no'. We have a huge base of 
public domain software that is with us since early 3.2 and was never 
recompiled. In general, 'old' software should run on 'new' systems.

Of course, you will need to install some specific runtime environments
(most notably FORTRAN) for dynamically linked software 
(commercial or your own) to be able to run.

In specific cases the answer can be 'hmmm' - you may have software that
relies on some specific version of a shared library ('bug's therein).
To keep these programs happy, you can try to recompile and link statically
on the 3.2 system.  
In most of these cases what is required is a patch to the sources. 
On other-not DU-platforms we have seen problems with programs like top
that needed updating of that kind.

Stefan.

