It's worse than that.  Even with plenty of O2 left to breath,
CO2 can mess you up bad.  IIRC, your body decides
when to take it's next breath based not on a lack of
oxygen in the blood, but on the build up of too much
CO2 in the blood.  So if the ambient CO2 concentration
gets too high, you'll start breathing very rapidly and
strenuously, which will cause you to hyperventilate
and pass out from too much O2 in the blood.

Weird, eh ?

There's also apparently problems with too much CO2
in the blood turning the blood acidic (carbonic acid,
like in soda pop, forms) and apparently that messes
things up too.

I'm on the hairy thin edge of my knowledge here; if
someone who knows better could correct any mistakes
I may have made, that would be a good thing.  Also
note that this is not really very computer related, but
it is interesting to the people here I hope.  Still, lets
no go on too much about it, please !
