  I'm sure someone else will comment on the legal issues surrounding this 8-(

  Both DECserver 200's use the same load image - PR0801ENG.SYS. The DECserver
500 doesn't have a single specific image - there's a configurator utility that
runs on the host system (I know there's one for VAX/VMS, and I'd presume that
there is one for RSX as well) which clones a generic image and applies the
user's config changes. This is because the DS500/550 are actually built out
of generic PDP-11 parts and don't have any EEPROM/NVRAM memory to store the
box config.

