Ah, a perfect subject for getting off the beaten path...

Back about 1969, the top-of-line Camp Trails pack frame was
made from a magnesium alloy, on the theory that this was a
significant source of weight reduction (it really was not).

I saw the remains of a magnesium pack frame that fell, by
one corner, into the hot embers of a campfire.  Essentially,
2/3 of the frame was missing -- completely gone.  I can 
imagine waking up at midnight and thinking, "boy, the moon sure
is bright tonight!"  Most back-packers don't carry metal-X
or Na2CO3, so I guess there wouldn't be much to do except
sit and watch the fireworks.



