Gary Heston wrote:
> For magnesium, water is an oxidizer...

That holds true for Al as well, which is why they galvanically bond Al
bars to ocean-going vessels:

It's better to sacrifice a few Al bars than to have uncontrolled rusting
of the steel.

Re. magnesium: It is possible to cast a kind of porous (spongelike) form
of magnesium by passing lots of gas bubbles through the solidifying
metal.

The resulting material has lots of interesting properties, but if you
put it in salt water it can corrode in literally no time. :-)

Terje

