I wrote a piece of Fortran 90 code that evaluates polynomials. The
code routinely runs at 95% or higher of the theoretical peak performance
of the floating point unit.  A uniprocessor 500 MHz Alpha (EV5 and EV6)
will execute well over 990 MFlops/sec.  I dont bother to count the integer
instruction execution rate.  I have seen 1584 MFlop/sec on an 800 MHz
system.

Although Alpha does not have a mull-add instruction, the compiler is
capable of generating full pipelined multiplies and adds to keep the FPU
pipeline bubble-less.

Don Dossa





