Aaron Spink wrote:
> 
> Libor <libor@tango.canis.uiuc.edu> writes:
> 
> > "Extinguishing magnesium fires presents special problems. Because
> 
> Anyone know the ignition point for magnesium?

I don't know the actual temperature, but I do know that a regular match
is hot enough.

Magnesium is hard to ignite however, unless you have it in a form with
very large specific surface area, i.e. shavings from a milling machine.

If you throw a handfull of that stuff into a hot oven, i.e. like a small
lab furnace, you can get a very satisfying flash. :-)

Terje

