On Fri, 19 Feb 1999, Brett Bensley wrote:

> I just inherited a DECStation 5000 and 3100.  I would like to get
> something running on them.  Need information about attaching a monitor

Which 5000? A 25 for example has on-board video, others use TURBOchannel
option modules like a PMAGB-BA. With a special DEC-cable you can hook
a monitor that syncs on green to one these mentioned.

> and keyboard...have a puck mouse.  Also, want to be able to install
> Linux or BSD on one...anyway to add a floppy drive?  Have expansion
> cases with SCSI drives in them.  Any information that would help me get
> these beasts running will be greatly appreciated.

Linux I would call still experimental, you need a terminal instead of
a monitor by lack of a video driver, if you're interested have a look
at http://decstation.unix-ag.org/

NetBSD runs stable on these beasts, look at http://www.netbsd.org/
for the pamx port.

With a SCSI to floppy interface you can add a floppydrive in any of
them, the Personal DECstation 5000/xx (xx being one of 20, 25, 33, 50)
has a on-board floppy controller.

Regards,
Richard




