|> has a on-board floppy controller.

Scsi floppies are supported as boot devices, if you can squeeze a
kernel onto one. (The distribution does not include a floppy boot
image, since scsi floppies are rare). Otherwise the recommended
install procedure is to net-boot.

Note that the 2.88 Mbyte floppy in Personal DECstations is not
supported as a boot device, at least not by any PROMs I've ever seen;
it's not supported by the released version of NetBSD, either.



