In article <36C7683C.FEDFC835@csi.com>, Keith Hayes <hayesk@csi.com> wrote:

>     I am looking into adding an external hard drive to my AlphaStation 200,
> and I am unsure if the SCSI bus is differential or single ended.  I  would
> assume single ended, but I would like to be sure.  Does anyone have
> an answer for me.

I have several of these units. The external connector is an extention of
the internal bus, and it is SCSI II. Differential drives will not work nor
will any other SCSI III or Ultra SCSI drive work without an adapter to
narrow 50-pin.

Hope this helps.

