I have an Ultra5 desktop and a E150 Server, the Desktop 
uses 10,000 RPM EIDE drives, the Server simular 10,000 RPM
SCSI drives, for sequential access the EIDE drives are 
actually slightly faster. For striped access to multiple 
drives the SCSI subsystem is quicker. 

But the Ultra5 is a workstation, it generally does not 
load its filesystem very heavily, the E150 on the other 
hand is a fileserver and is quite I/O bound.

I base this on running Virtual Adrian which tells me 
when I am stressing bits of each system.

So the basic point still applies.

Given that Ultra5's generally have one drive and 
ocasionally 2 when they are configured as workstations 
EIDE is not a bad choice.

Given that the E150 is a server sn if mainly I/O bound 
EIDE would be a bad choice.

