In article <tZ5w20pDAcxa084t2@u.ypcc.edu>, no@spam.thankyou (System Mangler) wrote:
>We got a couple of DEC 4000-610 systems from another department that
>we want to make into a 2 node cluster under VMS. One system has 5 SCSI
>busses, the second has 3 SCSI busses and 2 DSSI busses.  We were just going
>to connect a SCSI bus from each system to each other but we now know that
>these systems don't work in SCSI clusters.  Option 2 is to connect the
>systems together with a DSSI bus.  What needs to be done to "transplant"
>a DSSI bus from one system to the other (and a SCSI bus the other way I
>guess)?  They seem to be very interchangeable, the console doesn't even
>know what type of bus it is unless a disk is connected to it. VMS 6.2.

There are two kinds of DEC 4000 storage adapter: one has 4 Fast SCSI buses 
plus an ethernet port, the other has 4 DSSI/SCSI busses (each independently 
selectable) plus two ethernet ports. (At least this is what the tech manaul 
says - I don't play with DEC 4000s but I do have one in the lab to look at if 
you get stuck).

So your first step is to determine which if the two types of I/O controller 
you have in your system. (One of them obviously has at least one DSSI/SCSI 
controller but the other may well already have a SCSI/DSSI controller that 
happens to be set to all SCSI).

You will probably need to borrow or purchase the relevant manuals:

      EK-KN430-TM             DEC 4000 AXP Model 600 Series Tecnical Manual
      EK-KN430-SV             DEC 4000 AXP Model 600 Series Service Guide
      EK-KN430-IP              DEC 4000 Enclosures Illustrated Parts Breakdown

