In article <36c28a17.0@news.intercomm.com>, "Wayne Rigby" <metahawk@earthling.net> wrote:
>I am looking for information about creating utilities that run before the OS
>is booted on Alpha computers.  That is, to create something like the
>Mylex/KZPAC RAID configuration utility that one runs to configure the RAID
>array before the OS loads or is even installed in some cases.  From the
>ARC/AlphaBIOS there is a utility launch menu and I would imagine there is
>some way to run something from the SRM console.  Does anyone know of any
>SDKs or other sources of information regarding this sort of programming?
>

Start by picking up a Linux distribution for Alpha (sources, obviously) and 
look at milo - this is the bit that runs first and loads up Linux. Start with 
the micropal module and follow the code :-)

You will also need the hardware reference manual for whichever Alpha processor 
your system uses and the corresponding manual(s) for the system's chipset and 
any support chips you need to use. There is also usually a system technical 
manual which will help immensely in piecing it all together.

