> Sounds like a good idea to me, but how about taking it up a layer and
> resurrecting the old ucsd p-code idea from a decade ago ?. With modern
> cpu speeds, probably wouldn't be a serious performance hit for many
> applications.

Architecture-independent software delivery has been resurrected
recently.  It is called the Java byte-code engine.  You can use
it for programs written in Java.  You can also use it for programs
written in Ada.  I have no idea how many other languages have
compilers that emit Java byte-code.

Larry Kilgallen



