It's quite some time since I last booted a 8700, but if I remember
correctly the Pro380 has the command files to boot the VAX on it's
harddisk. You can set up various boot files for standard,
conversational, or standalone backup boot but they must reflect your
8700 configuration (unit number of disk to boot from, and/or number(s)
of HSC(s) to access these disks etc. I believe these command files set
the proper register values and then boot the VAX. It saves you a lot
of typing.

I don't remember how you got to the OS prompt of the Pro380 to edit
these files... 

