  Hrm..  I don't think so, but I'm not sure which Mac problems
you're specifically thinking of.  An Alpha motherboard is very 
PC-board-like.  You put it in a standard case and plug standard
PCI and ISA devices into it, then you either run WNT or Linux on
it.

  If x86 execution performance is a big issue, then you'd put an
AMD K7 on it.  If getting maximum performance is a big issue and 
you either have sources, or are running legacy Alpha binaries, or 
can get it your application precompiled for Alpha, then you'd put 
a 21264 on it.  Either way you can expect x86 to "just work" -- 
natively on the K7 or via FX!32 on the Alpha.

