(Date math is probably off by a day or so to make round numbers.)

3Q98 = Sept 30th, 1998
4Q99 = Dec 31st, 1999

455 days / -$8,000 = -$17.58/day.

Lets say we are 130 days from "3Q98". ($10,000) - ($17.58 * 130) = $7,714,
which isn't very far from the truth.  (As in I think you might be able to
get that price. I'm certainly you could with a 30day delivery time :-))

So interpret this one of two ways:
    They haven't lied yet.
or:
    The original claim is just as implausible now as it was then.

Note that there was a slight delay off 3Q98 for availability of the type of
system being quoted. (I.e. I don't think you could buy the above for $10k
on Sept 30, 1998.) And the actually price is rather sensitive to the
performance of the competition. (Compaq and Samsung have much higher margin
at the start of the time period than they do at the end.) This is a double
edged sword because if there is no competition to the 21264, its price will
stay higher. I'm not terribly worried about this being the case though.

-Z-



