wisskirc@avzw02.physik.uni-bonn.de writes:

>Now the machine runs up normally for between 10 to 60 minutes,
>then it hangs up completely. The only recourse is the reset button.
>One finds a bunch of the following error messages:

>vmunix: svcktcp_reply: mbuf_send returned 32
>vmunix: rfs_dispatch: sendreply failed

The 32 is an errno value, in this case EPIPE.  It sounds like a NFS
client is closing a TCP connection in the midst of an operation.  (It
could be a Digital UNIX client).  If you are doing a lot of NFS over
UDP serving, you may be hitting a memory leak that involves duplicate
requests.  nfsstat, netstat, vmstat, tcpdump are all helpful tools, but
I'd start with the memory leak.  BL11 of the support pool fixes a lot
of the problem, BL12 fixes the rest.

	-Ric Werme
