>The LN03 uses the Ricoh 4081 engine.   From the Ricoh LP4081 IV2
>Technical Manual (page VII-3, section 7-1-2):
>
>    1.  Fusing system system error
>    2.  Optical system system error
>    3.  Numbers 1 and 2 occur
>    4.  OPC synchronous mark error
>    5.  Numbers 1 and 4 occur
>    6.  Numbers 2 and 4 occur
>    7.  Numbers 1, 2 and 4 occur
>    8.  Main motor error
>    9.  Numbers 1 and 8 occur
>    A.  Numbers 2 and 8 occur
>    B.  Numbers 1, 2 and 8 occur
>    F.  Engine drive board memory error
>
>OPC Synchronous Mark Error:  This error occurs if the OPC
>mark is not detected within 7.5 seconds after issuance of
>the main motor drive signal or if the next OPC mark is not
>detected within 7.5 seconds after the detection of the first
>OPC mark.
>
>Possible problems/solutions for OPC errors are:
>
>OPC cartridge inserted properly?
>OPC sensor dirty?
>OPC mark missing or covered by dirt?
>OPC MRK signal OK?   (If yes, replace the engine drive board)
>OPC cartridge driven correctly?  (If no, check drive gears/belt tension)
>OPC belt slipping?  (If yes, replace OPC.   If no, replace OPC sensor)
>
>If it is a drive gear problem, let me know.   I have a few
>spares, if you can identify which one is bad.
>
