It's really hard to say without actually running your code across different
platforms.  You could get a 21164 500MHz Alpha for under $2500 if you
configure it right.  If you have a lot of codes to run at the same time,
you might get better through put from a dual processor PII.  So my answer
to you is "it depends".  Right now our 21164 533MHz Alphas are under 2x
the speed of our 400MHz PIIs when running our FP heavy Monte Carlo simulation
codes. 

