The NetApp boxes use 400 or 600 Mhz 21164 Alpha CPU's running a custom 
os with a custom filesystem called WAFL. The NetAPP is as its 
name suggests a Network Appliance it does not run applications 
just filesystems and is therefore not going to broaden the Alpha 
applications base any more than Auspex who use SPARC CPUs are going 
to increase the SPARC/Solaris applications base.

NetAPP produce small, plug and go NFS fileservers. They have also 
been sucessfull but the volumes of NetApp filers are hardly going 
to make a dent in the Alpha market even when marketed by Dell.  

