Subject: ATI Mach64 ISA video card in AlphaServer 400 with Dec Unix 4.0d
Date: 1999/02/01
Message-ID: <7959o4$nhn$1@remarQ.com>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 439529233
X-MimeOLE: Produced By Microsoft MimeOLE V4.72.3110.3
X-Complaints-To: newsabuse@remarQ.com
X-Trace: 917908036 H0GVAKYFN425ED0C C usenet80.supernews.com
Organization: Compuflight, Inc
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec

We recently ran into a problem that I was not able to resolve with FAQs or
postings, so I thought I would post it for future use if someone has a
similar problem.

The ISA/PCI bus version of the AlphaServer 400 was often sold with the ATI
Mach64 ISA video option. upgrading to version 4.0 from 3.2 Dec Unix might
disable this beast for anything other than generic VGA use. All
documentation we had was either related to setting the ISA card up on DEC
3.2, or setting up the EISA version on DEC 4.0. Nothing refered to setting
up the ISA version of the video card on 4.0 for this (old) alpha box.

To setup the ATI Mach64 ISA card on the alphaserver with DEC 4.0 unix, you
must go into the SRM and add the card as a 'MACH64' with the enabled option
to 'Y'. This can be done with iconfig or isaconfig at the >>> prompt. (our
documentation refered to it as ISA--VGA as the name, it must be set to
MACH64, that was the kicker)

reboot, rebuild the kernal and viola, the ATI is back and available to X in
higher res modes.

If anyone has questions, feel free to mail me or post.

RoBaer  rstewart@gwdi.com






