There are a number of issues with reference to SPEC scores for the
21164 Alpha.  First, the fastest 21164s run at 667 Mhz and not 600
Mhz.  Second, 21164 systems are available with L2 cache of 2,4, and 8
MB.

According to http://www.dcginc.com/1999/fr_lx_series.html,
A 667 Mhz 21164 w/4 MB L2 has a SPECint of 23.0.  I'm a little
skeptical that this is accurate since they (and others I have seen;
i.e. Microway) list the 633 Mhz w/4 MB at 19.0.  Simple extrapolation
would put the 667 Mhz 21164 at about 20 or so.

<snip>


