Hi there.  I'm looking for a disk enclosure system that is kind of
like Digital StorageWorks, but that allows me to use non-DEC drives,
particularly Seagates (Seagate Barracude 4GB drives in particular).

Our situation is that we currently have four Ultra SCSI chains
consisting of between four and seven drives each, with each drive in
its own separate enclosure.  This, as you can imagine, is a bit of a 
nightmare in terms of SCSI chain lengths and cable hassles.  But I 
don't want to give up the fact that is is easy to swap single drives 
in and out of the chain.

What I want is to take my Seagates out of their enclosures, mount them 
into some kind of carriers or caddies, which in turn slots into some kind 
of main enclosure.

I do not need true hot-swap capability -- if I have to cut power to 
the enclosure to swap out drives, that's fine.  I just want it to be 
easy to swap out drives in their caddies.  And I'm assuming that all 
drives in a single such enclosure must be on the same SCSI chain.

If possible, I would like to find such an enclosure that is either 
rackmount or in a tower, that can hold four disks or more each.

If anyone has any suggestions, either for particular products or for 
vendors that I ought to be contacting, please let me know.  Thanks!

