Organization: /usr/lib/news/organi[sz]ation
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


We're having more problems with our routeabout bridged network.  The net
consists of 8 routeabout EWs, a central with 7 inbound frame ports and a
remote for each of those frame ports; all links are 56KB, the central
router comes in via a 512K fractional T1.  All links are currently running
transparent bridge to support LAT, NETbios filtering is enabled on all
links, IP is not filtered (will soon be routed, but not now).

One of the links keeps going down.  When it happens, the frame console
shows the link as down on both remote and the central router (the one 
PVC is down from the central's point of view).  We have had the carrier
testing the lines for days and they claim no fault.  None of the other
lines goes down.  All equipment self tests just fine (we're putting in
a spare CSU at the remote tomorrow; don't have a spare router)

We have so far had 100% success in restoring the link simply by restarting
the remote routeabout, _or_ the central routeabout, _or_ running a line
test on the CSU (which seems to cause the router to reset the frame port).
We have so far been unable to capture any meaningful error messages from
the router console port.

The funny thing is another customer site (using V2.05 software; the current
customer is at V3.0.1) had almost identical problems over one of their
three frame links (though far less frequent); we were never able to 
trace the problem, but it became infrequent enough to not be a critical
issue (and easily, if inelegantly, user-correctable).

Any ideas would be appreciated.  Any pointers towards good books or
other material to better understand these routers and the more-or-less
standard 'standards' that the bridging runs over also appreciated (the
docs are not really all that revealing for troubleshooting things like
this...

Thanks...

Rich Jordan
rjordan@mcs.net




