Timothy Cullip <cullip@radonc.unc.edu> wrote:
: I'm looking for information on the newly announced XP1000.

: 1) The web page mentions that it uses 100 MHz Registered ECC SDRAM.
: Is the memory bus really running at 100 MHz? I believe it is 256

The XP10000 memory bus runs at 83 Mhz, the new EV57 board (newest
21164pc revision) runs at 75 Mhz.

The XP1000 has 4 seperate 64 bit system busses, with a sustained
available bandwidth of over 2.6 GB/sec.  Sounds like a never to
exceed burst number to me (4 64 bit busses * 83 Mhz = 2656 MB/sec).

So it's organized as 2 banks of 4 dimms, not sure if having
1 or 2 banks effects the memory system performance.

The memory dimms are compatible with SP700 (x86) which I think means
they are PC100 ECC registered.  I.e. $245 per 128 MB at 
www.thechipmerchant.com.  If so sounds like great news to me.

: 2) Anyone have any memory throughput information on the XP1000. I'm
: especially interested in the stream benchmark. It would be nice if
: it were about as fast as the DS20 (about 1000 Mbytes/sec on the
: stream benchmark).

I'd be very interested in similiar, as well as dual cpu numbers
for the XP1000.

: 3) Any other information not readily available from Compaq's web site
: would be appriciated.

There are two technical white papers under technical manuals on the compaq
XP1000 product pages.  Glad to see that compaq isn't afraid to brag
about some of the technical details.


--
Bill 



